---
/**
 * Data Packs Hub Page
 */
import BaseHead from "../../components/BaseHead.astro"
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro"
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro"
import LoadingBar from "../../components/LoadingBar.astro"
import Breadcrumb from "../../components/Breadcrumb.astro"
import "@fontsource/ubuntu"
import "@fontsource/ubuntu/500.css"
import "@fontsource/ubuntu/700.css"

Astro.locals.cache(300)
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Minecraft Data Packs | GDLauncher"
      description="Browse and install Minecraft data packs from CurseForge and Modrinth. Add new recipes and mechanics without mods."
      keywords="minecraft data packs, curseforge datapacks, modrinth datapacks, vanilla tweaks, gdlauncher"
    />
  </head>

  <body class="bg-darkSlate-900 text-lightSlate-50 min-h-screen">
    <LoadingBar />
    <!-- Background layers -->
    <div class="fixed inset-0 -z-10">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_60%_40%_at_50%_0%,rgba(43,107,177,0.12),transparent)]"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.02)_1px,transparent_1px),linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(255,255,255,0.02)_1px,transparent_1px)] bg-[size:64px_64px]"></div>
    </div>
    <Header />

    <main class="py-8">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: "Data Packs" }]} maxWidth="max-w-6xl" />

      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="bg-darkSlate-800 rounded-xl p-8 md:p-12 mb-12">
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-lightSlate-50 mb-4">
            Minecraft
            <span class="text-primary-300">Data Packs</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100 text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            Data packs add new recipes, loot tables, and game mechanics to vanilla Minecraft.
            No mods required - works natively with the game.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-lightSlate-50">What are Data Packs?</h2>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Data packs are a vanilla Minecraft feature that lets you customize game behavior.
            They're perfect for adding tweaks without needing a mod loader.
          </p>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">Data packs can modify:</p>
          <ul class="text-darkSlate-100">
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Crafting Recipes</strong> - Add or change how items are crafted</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Loot Tables</strong> - Modify what mobs drop and chest contents</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Advancements</strong> - Add custom achievements and rewards</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">World Generation</strong> - Change biome distribution and structures</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Functions</strong> - Run commands automatically</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-lightSlate-50">Data Packs vs Mods</h2>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Data packs and mods serve different purposes:
          </p>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100"><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Data Packs:</strong></p>
          <ul class="text-darkSlate-100">
            <li>Drop directly into your world folder - no mod loader needed</li>
            <li>Limited to vanilla mechanics (can't add new blocks or mobs)</li>
            <li>Only needed on the server - clients stay vanilla</li>
            <li>Usually survive Minecraft updates without breaking</li>
            <li>Minimal performance impact</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100"><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Mods:</strong></p>
          <ul class="text-darkSlate-100">
            <li>Require a mod loader (Forge, Fabric, etc.)</li>
            <li>Can add entirely new content, mechanics, and systems</li>
            <li>Usually needed on both server and client</li>
            <li>Often break when Minecraft updates until the author patches them</li>
            <li>Can significantly impact performance</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Data packs are perfect for vanilla-compatible tweaks. Use mods when you need entirely new content or mechanics.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-lightSlate-50">Full Capabilities</h2>
          <p class="text-darkSlate-100">
            Data packs can modify many vanilla systems. Introduced in Minecraft 1.13 (2018), they're officially supported by Mojang:
          </p>
          <ul class="text-darkSlate-100">
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Recipes</strong> - Add new crafting recipes or modify existing ones</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Loot tables</strong> - Change mob drops, chest contents, fishing loot</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Advancements</strong> - Create custom achievements with rewards</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">World generation</strong> - Modify biome placement, structures, ore distribution</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Functions</strong> - Run command sequences (like command blocks, but file-based)</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Predicates</strong> - Create complex conditions for game events</li>
            <li><strong class="text-lightSlate-50">Tags</strong> - Group blocks/items for consistent behavior</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <div class="bg-darkSlate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center">
            <div class="p-8 lg:p-12">
              <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-lightSlate-50 mb-4">Browse Data Packs in GDLauncher</h2>
              <p class="text-darkSlate-100 mb-6">
                Find and install data packs from CurseForge and Modrinth directly in GDLauncher.
                Enhance vanilla Minecraft without needing mods.
              </p>
              <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 mb-8">
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-darkSlate-50">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-400 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                  <span>Browse data packs from CurseForge & Modrinth</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-darkSlate-50">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-400 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                  <span>Works with vanilla Minecraft - no mods required</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-darkSlate-50">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary-400 flex-shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                  <span>Easy installation and management</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
              <a href="/download/windows" data-astro-prefetch="false" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-primary-500 hover:bg-primary-600 text-lightSlate-50 font-semibold transition-colors transition-transform duration-100 ease-spring active:scale-95">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M3 12V6.75l6-1.32v6.48L3 12zm17-9v8.75l-10 .15V5.21L20 3zM3 13l6 .09v6.81l-6-1.15V13zm17 .25V22l-10-1.91V13.1l10 .15z"/></svg>
                Download GDLauncher
              </a>
            </div>
            <div class="relative">
              <img
                src="https://cdn.gdl.gg/assets/website-browse-datapacks.jpg"
                alt="GDLauncher data pack browser interface"
                class="w-full h-auto"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8 bg-darkSlate-800 rounded-xl p-8 md:p-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-lightSlate-50 mb-6 text-center">Learn More</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          <a href="/guides/install-datapacks" class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-darkSlate-700/50 hover:bg-darkSlate-700 transition-colors transition-transform duration-100 ease-spring active:scale-98">
            <span class="text-lightSlate-50 font-medium">How to Install Data Packs</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/guides/install-mods" class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-darkSlate-700/50 hover:bg-darkSlate-700 transition-colors transition-transform duration-100 ease-spring active:scale-98">
            <span class="text-lightSlate-50 font-medium">How to Install Mods</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
